# Convert MVT Python Project into a Single EXE

I want to package my MVT Python project into one standalone Windows executable named `MVT.exe`, without an `_internal` folder.

## 1. Open CMD

```cmd
cd /d D:\minimax\mass_visitor_tool
```

## 2. Install dependencies

```cmd
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pip install pyinstaller
```

## 3. Clean previous builds

```cmd
rmdir /s /q build
rmdir /s /q dist
del /q MVT.spec
```

## 4. Build the EXE

```cmd
python -m PyInstaller --onefile --windowed --name MVT --clean --noconfirm main.py
```

## 5. Check output

```cmd
dir dist
```

Expected output:

```text
MVT/
└── dist/
    └── MVT.exe
```

## 6. Test the EXE

```cmd
dist\MVT.exe
```

## Important Requirements

- The EXE must include all required Python modules.
- Preserve PyQt6 GUI functionality.
- Ensure Playwright integration works.
- Handle Playwright browser binaries separately if necessary.
- Preserve configuration and logging functionality.
- Fix missing DLL and module errors.
- Do not delete or modify the original Python source code.
- Test the EXE on a Windows computer without Python installed.

## 7. If the EXE fails

Run:

```cmd
python -m PyInstaller --onefile --console --name MVT_Debug --clean --noconfirm main.py
```

Then run:

```cmd
dist\MVT_Debug.exe
```

Use the error messages to identify missing dependencies and fix the build configuration.

**Final goal:** A working single-file `MVT.exe` that users can run without installing Python or Python packages.
